# DigitalOcean Nodes — Datachain Rope (2026-05-03)

## Topology

The Datachain Rope mainnet (chainId 271828) now runs across **4 production blue-green slots** + **2 Quipu Canon knot witnesses** spanning 2 cloud providers and 2 regions:

| Role | Hostname | Provider | Region | IP | Disk | RAM | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **BLUE (primary)** | `dcrope` | Gandi | Paris SD6 | `92.243.26.189` | 484 GB | 8 GB | active sequencer; Reth produces blocks |
| **GREEN (secondary)** | `dcrope-node2` | Gandi | Paris SD6 | `92.243.25.119` | — | 8 GB | hot-warm spare; receives state-sync from BLUE every 15 min (`*/15 * * * *`) |
| **DO rpc-1 (tertiary)** | `datachain-rpc-1` | DigitalOcean | Frankfurt (fra1) | `157.230.18.45` | 78 GB | 3.8 GB + 4 GB swap | hot-warm spare; receives state-sync from BLUE every 15 min (offset `7,22,37,52`) |
| **DO rpc-2 (quaternary)** | `datachain-rpc-2` | DigitalOcean | Frankfurt (fra1) | `167.172.106.174` | 78 GB | 3.8 GB + 4 GB swap | hot-warm spare; receives state-sync from rpc-1 every 15 min (offset `12,27,42,57`) |
| **Witness 1** | `datachain-validator-1` | DigitalOcean | Frankfurt (fra1) | `159.89.3.160` | 25 GB | 1 GB | rope-node only (no Reth); `mode=validator`, `[consensus] enabled=true`; produces local anchors, ready for Testimony Consensus |
| **Witness 2** | `datachain-validator-2` | DigitalOcean | Frankfurt (fra1) | `159.65.119.231` | 25 GB | 1 GB | same as witness 1; paired |

All 4 RPC slots share **identical genesis hash** `0x6a425482c849cfa07ec253c272a661375469b71c47f499048218a377a24d7203` and `chainId 0x425d4 (271828)`. Witnesses also report the same `eth_chainId` because they delegate to `https://erpc.datachain.network` via `[evm_backend]`.

## Public RPC failover order

Nginx upstream `digitalocean_rpc` (legacy name preserved for stability) on BLUE:

```nginx
upstream digitalocean_rpc {
    server host.docker.internal:8545 max_fails=2 fail_timeout=5s;  # BLUE primary
    server 92.243.25.119:8545 backup;                              # GREEN secondary
    server 157.230.18.45:8545 backup;                              # DO rpc-1 tertiary (2026-05-03)
    server 167.172.106.174:8545 backup;                            # DO rpc-2 quaternary (2026-05-03)
}
```

Public traffic via `https://erpc.datachain.network` flows: **BLUE → GREEN if BLUE down → rpc-1 if both Gandi down → rpc-2 if all three down**.

## DO RPC slot services (rpc-1, rpc-2)

Each DO RPC node runs the same 3-service stack as BLUE/GREEN:

| Service | Port | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `reth-rope.service` | 8595 (private) | Reth v1.11.2 EVM backend in `--dev --dev.block-time 3s` mode |
| `datachain-rope.service` | 8545 (firewalled) | rope-node serving Quipu Canon v1.1 RPC (`rope_*` + `eth_*` aliases) |
| `dc-explorer.service` | 3001 (private) | DCScan explorer API (read-through to local rope-node) |

## Witness services (validator-1, validator-2)

Witness nodes do **not** run Reth (insufficient disk for full chain DB). They run a single service:

| Service | Port | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `datachain-rope.service` | 8545 (firewalled), 9000 (libp2p public) | rope-node in `mode=validator` with `[consensus] enabled=true`. Produces local anchors via `string_producer`. Delegates `eth_*` to `https://erpc.datachain.network` via `[evm_backend]`. |
| `dc-explorer.service` | 3001 (private) | DCScan explorer API |

Witness config: `deploy/config/rope-witness.toml`. Witness systemd unit: `deploy/datachain-rope-witness.service` (installed on the host as `/etc/systemd/system/datachain-rope.service`).

## Firewall (UFW) — every DO node

| Port | Allowed sources | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `22/tcp` | Anywhere | SSH |
| `9000` | Anywhere (witnesses only) | rope-node libp2p (public for peer discovery) |
| `8545` (rope-node RPC) | BLUE, GREEN, all other DO nodes (mutual) | private mesh |
| `8595` (Reth RPC) | BLUE, GREEN, all other RPC slots (rpc-1↔rpc-2) | private mesh; not opened on witnesses (no Reth) |
| `3001` (dc-explorer) | BLUE only | management plane |

Public internet **cannot** reach DO RPC ports — only the Gandi infrastructure (which hosts `erpc.datachain.network` nginx) plus the DO peer mesh can reach DO RPC ports.

## State-sync mechanism

Three scripts in `/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/`:

### `reth-do-sync.sh <target-ip>` — routine BLUE → DO RPC slot (cron, 15 min)

Hot rsync from BLUE → DO. **BLUE never stops.** DO Reth is briefly stopped for the rsync window (~30-60 s) to avoid mdbx concurrent-write corruption on destination. Then verifies block height + deployer nonce match.

- Cron on BLUE (ubuntu): `7,22,37,52 * * * * reth-do-sync.sh >> .../reth-do-sync.log` (defaults to rpc-1 = 157.230.18.45)
- Parameterized: pass an IP arg to target other DO nodes

### `reth-do-peer-sync.sh user@host` — DO peer (rpc-1 → rpc-2) every 15 min

Pattern: **stop-tar-stream-restart** (safe even with `--dev` divergent chains). Briefly stops the LOCAL Reth (~30-60 s) to take a consistent MDBX snapshot, tar-streams over the DO-internal network (fra1↔fra1, ~80 MB/s), then both restart. Safe because rpc-1 is itself a backup (no public traffic).

- Cron on rpc-1 (root): `12,27,42,57 * * * * reth-do-peer-sync.sh root@167.172.106.174 >> /var/log/reth-do-peer-sync.log`
- Why DO→DO and not BLUE→rpc-2 hot rsync? Empirical (2026-05-03): hot rsync of a *full bootstrap* corrupts mdbx because each Reth node runs `--dev` with its own divergent block sequence; the rsync overlay merges inconsistent MDBX pages. Stop-tar-stream-restart on a backup source is safer and stays out of BLUE.

### `reth-do-bootstrap.sh [target-ip]` — recovery (manual, BLUE → DO)

Used only when DO mdbx is corrupt or empty AND no DO peer can supply a snapshot. Briefly stops BLUE (~3-4 min), streams an uncompressed tar, restarts both. GREEN takes over public traffic during BLUE's stop window. Defaults to rpc-1; pass an IP for other targets.

