## Cost / operational notes

- No DigitalOcean LB in front of DO droplets — saves ~$10/month. Failover is handled by Gandi nginx upstream.
- All 6 nodes (4 RPC + 2 witnesses) are now in productive use; no idle billable resources to destroy.

## Operational runbook

| Scenario | Action |
|---|---|
| BLUE Reth crashes | GREEN auto-takes traffic via nginx; bring BLUE back; sync resumes |
| BLUE + GREEN both down | rpc-1 auto-takes traffic via nginx; fix Gandi infra |
| All Gandi + rpc-1 down | rpc-2 auto-takes traffic via nginx |
| DO rpc-1 mdbx corrupted | `ssh rope-vps '/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/reth-do-bootstrap.sh'` (briefly stops BLUE, streams clean snapshot) |
| DO rpc-2 mdbx corrupted | `ssh root@157.230.18.45 '/opt/datachain-rope/scripts/reth-do-peer-sync.sh root@167.172.106.174'` (briefly stops rpc-1, no public impact) |
| Witness needs reset | `ssh root@<witness-ip> 'systemctl stop datachain-rope; rm -rf /home/ubuntu/.rope/mainnet/db/*; systemctl start datachain-rope'` |
| Decommission a node | Remove from nginx upstream, remove cron entry, `doctl droplet delete` (requires DO API token) |
